From a39e9104ed9863741451ec475d835b9bbd08992f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 14:21:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2162/2165] media: i2c: vd55g0: register as a sensor subdevice

Use v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor() so the V4L2 core looks up the
sensor's privacy LED and other sensor firmware properties, and lights the
LED while the sensor streams. With plain v4l2_async_register_subdev() a
privacy LED described for the IR camera was never used.

Tested on a Microsoft Surface Pro 11 (X1E80100): the camera privacy LED
now lights while the IR camera streams.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
(cherry picked from commit 169be80a541b106e57f8f9d3a92eb9a18003b58a)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0.c b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0.c
index 98918ecd6e8a85b0f49d4da77aaa98596b17f44a..a62a99f40ba48b03c29e0f082c0f43fea5445b5c 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/vd55g0.c
@@ -1928,7 +1928,7 @@ static int vd55g0_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	pm_runtime_get_noresume(dev);
 	pm_runtime_enable(dev);
 
-	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev(&sensor->sd);
+	ret = v4l2_async_register_subdev_sensor(&sensor->sd);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(&client->dev, "async subdev register failed %d", ret);
 		goto error_pm_runtime;
